    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T16:31:54Z",
    "body": "The maintainer said in chat on 2026-11-22: \"Wopr has been labeled.\"\n\nChecked at the API at 16:33Z: the runner `wopr` is online and its labels are `camcraft-post-merge` and `camcraft-cut`. The `needs-maintainer` label is removed, because the owner step is done.\n\nThis issue stays open for the last point of \"Done means\": a `dry_run` cut (or the next real cut) must start on `wopr`. Start it when no post-merge run is in progress (a cut yields the runner; a run now would delay the post-merge gates): `gh workflow run cut.yml -f version=<next> -f stage=gate -f dry_run=true`. When the run starts on `wopr`, the stop-gap of #3269 (pausing the other post-merge runners while a release PR is open) can be retired, and this issue closes.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
